            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "procedures/phal/enter_mpreboot.cpp",
                    "line": 144,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "Please use `pdbg_set_loglevel(getLogLevelFromEnv(\"PDBG_LOG\", PDBG_INFO))` so that the log level can be controlled dynamically via the PDBG_LOG environment variable, avoiding the need to recompile the code when debugging traces needed from the PHAL layer.\n\nWhy are we using `PDBG_NOTICE` as log level than PDBG_INFO (which is the default level)?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "procedures/phal/enter_mpreboot.cpp",
                    "line": 149,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "FYI, if you want PHAL traces to be captured in the PEL\u2014similar to how it's done for the Start Host command\u2014you'll need to set up a corresponding callback. I assume you're aiming to improve debuggability with these changes, so just sharing this for your reference."
                }
            ],
